Fix: if frame not in _vel_dict, compute velocity via self.vel(frame)? Better: use `if frame in self._vel_dict: return self._vel_dict[frame].dt(frame)` else compute via self.vel(frame).dt(frame)? Actually proper behavior: acceleration = derivative of velocity. If vel missing, compute velocity using vel(frame) which auto-computes. Simplest:

```
if not (frame in self._acc_dict):
    if frame in self._vel_dict:
        return self._vel_dict[frame].dt(frame)
    return self.vel(frame).dt(frame)
```

But issue says "if computed velocity is zero, acceleration set to zero". vel(frame) computation may set _vel_dict. Use that.

